\id PHM Original Douay-Rheims (1582/1610)
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Philemon
\toc1 The Epistle of Paul to Philemon.
\toc2 Philemon
\toc3 PHM
\mt1 The Epistle of Paul to Philemon.
\c 1
\cd Hearing of Philemon's virtue, who was a Colossian, he writeth a familiar letter from Rome (being prisoner there) about his fugitive servant Onesimus: not doubting but that he might command him, yet rather requesting that he will forgive him, yea and receive him as he would Paul himself, who also hopeth to come unto him.
\p
\v 1 \sc Paul\sc* the prisoner of Christ \sc Jesus\sc*, and brother Timothee: to Philemon the beloved and our coadjutor,
\v 2 and to Appia our dearest sister, and to Archippus our fellow-soldier and to the church which is in thy house.
\v 3 Grace to you and peace from God our Father, and our Lord \sc Jesus\sc* Christ.
\v 4 I give thanks to my God, always making a memory of thee in my prayers,
\v 5 hearing thy \f 1 \fr 1.5 \ft Faith and charity commended always together, both necessary to make a complete Christian man, and to justification & salvation.\f* charity & faith which thou hast in our Lord \sc Jesus\sc*, and toward all the saints: \ef - \fr 1.5 \fq Toward all the saints. \ft ¹ The Apostle sticketh not to say, Charity and faith in Christ and all his Saints, which our captious Adversaries count in Catholic men's speeches and writings, very absurd, feigning that in all such we make no difference betwixt the love we bear to Christ, and the love we owe to our neighbours: betwixt the trust or belief we have in God, and that which we have in his holy Saints. Malice and contention doth so blind all Heretics. \fq ¹ \ft Faith and belief in Saints.\ef*
\v 6 that the communication of thy faith may be made evident in the agnition of all \f 1 \fr 1.6 \ft \+it * good work\+it*\f* good that is in you in Christ \sc Jesus\sc*.
\v 7 For I have had great joy and consolation in thy charity, because the bowels of the saints \f 1 \fr 1.7 \ft The duties of charity and mercy done to Christ's prisoners, are exceeding acceptable to God and all good men.\f* have rested by thee brother.
\v 8 For the which thing having great confidence in Christ \sc Jesus\sc* to command thee that which pertaineth to the purpose:
\v 9 for charity rather I beseech, whereas thou art such an one, as Paul being old and now prisoner also of \sc Jesus\sc* Christ.
\v 10 I beseech thee for my son whom I have begotten in bands, \x - \xt Col. 4, 9.\x* Onesimus,
\v 11 who hath been sometime unprofitable to thee, but now profitable both to me and thee,
\v 12 whom I have sent back to thee. And \f 1 \fr 1.12 \ft All Spiritual men ought to be exceeding propense and ready to procure men's pardon, and reconciliation to all penitents.\f* do thou receive him as mine own bowels.
\v 13 Whom I would have retained with me, that for thee he might minister to me in the bands of the Gospel:
\v 14 but without thy counsel I would do nothing: that thy good might be not as it were of necessity, but voluntary.
\v 15 For perhaps therefore he departed for a season from thee, that thou mightest take him again for ever.
\v 16 Now not as a servant, but for a servant, a most dear brother, especially to me, but how much more to thee both in the flesh and in our Lord?
\v 17 If therefore thou take me for thy fellow; receive him as myself.
\v 18 And if he hath hurt thee any thing or is in thy debt, that impute to me.
\v 19 I Paul have written with mine own hand: I will repay it: not to say to thee, \f 1 \fr 1.19 \ft The great debt & duty that we owe to such as be our spiritual parents in Christ.\f* that thou owest me thine own self also.
\v 20 Yea brother. \f 1 \fr 1.20 \ft \+it c ὀναίμησ\+it*\f* God grant I may enjoy thee in our Lord. Refresh my bowels in our Lord.
\v 21 Trusting in thy obedience I have written to thee, knowing that thou wilt do above that also which I do say.
\v 22 And withal provide me also a lodging. For I hope by your prayers that I shall be given to you.
\v 23 There salute thee Epaphras my fellow-prisoner in Christ \sc Jesus\sc*,
\v 24 Mark, Aristarchus, Demas and Luke my coadjutors.
\v 25 The grace of our Lord \sc Jesus\sc* Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
